From: wzdddyy <89689685+wzdddyy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: nf_conntrack: guard NULL exp_event callback

nf_ct_expect_event_report() calls notify->exp_event() without checking that
it is non-NULL, relying on every notifier registrant to populate both
callbacks. Out-of-tree notifiers (such as the QCA NSS ECM stack) only
provide .ct_event, so any expect event delivered while such a notifier is
installed jumps to NULL.

Observed on IPQ6018 (Link NN6000) with the NSS ECM stack: plugging in the
WAN cable makes tailscaled emit a UDP probe, conntrack raises an expect
event, and the kernel oopses with "pc : 0x0" inside
nf_ct_expect_event_report+0x80.

Guard the callback the same way the event path already is.

Signed-off-by: wzdddyy <89689685+wzdddyy@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_ecache.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_ecache.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_ecache.c
@@ -254,6 +254,7 @@ void nf_ct_expect_event_report(enum ip_conntrack_expect_events event,
 			.portid	= portid,
 			.report = report
 		};
+		if (notify->exp_event)
 		notify->exp_event(1 << event, &item);
 	}
 out_unlock:
